#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:5
#: 208e8aeac7e94eb5b66d4f2f2cbd6541
msgid "Setup Guide for Parrot Disco"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:10
#: a27177fb9f004a15bf59997b54d31b86
msgid "The Parrot Disco is a lightweight delta-wing with built-in camera and good flight characteristics. This page will help you get setup with ArduPilot running on your Disco."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:15
#: a67c41ceb41c46e58726ac9bedd4a63b
msgid "Prebuilt Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:17
#: 7dc6c0d06cbb4fae978ddc65d5bec7ae
msgid "A build of APM:Plane for Disco is automatically generated by the ArduPilot autobuild system. You can see the builds here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:20
#: 60b879b0b9314e75a2e6d2b5bf2f8536
msgid "https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Plane/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:22
#: 2b3bb7cc9859479aacfff584fb322dd2
msgid "the file you need to download is 'arduplane'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:25
#: 1c342005d4174c278a073d1b377dd2a4
msgid "Building Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:27
#: d814358de49a4857abf947d5b041dd3b
msgid "To build the ArduPilot firmware yourself you should use the waf build system, which is included as part of ArduPilot. The command to build APM:Plane for Disco is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:31
#: f869c49d254c43549ac6018b783ff109
msgid "``./waf configure --board disco``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:32
#: 4c6df908470943d1b7aaf91c9d75c9e3
msgid "``./waf plane``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:34
#: 48740fdeec494e7ba4b740978c836db1
msgid "this will give you a file build/disco/bin/arduplane that needs to be installed on your Disco."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:38
#: 9b4bdc189e35473e906413831961da42
msgid "Networking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:40
#: 52f2c0d52b134c788522bd5b434d3005
msgid "The Disco has a builtin WiFi access point, which will show up on your network as \"DISCO-xxxxxx\" where xxxxxx is a device specific serial number. The WiFi has no password by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:44
#: dd811553b97f4500ac553ed702d2e69a
msgid "You can also use USB networking if your operating system supports it. Just plug a USB cable into the left most USB port on the back of the CHUCK module and connect with your operating systems network manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:50
#: 7b3970c2947849b99046b9ced0dfe2ad
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:52
#: 3a9d1c52222d40fa939afe825d3e86c1
msgid "ArduPilot is usually installed in /data/ftp/internal_000/APM. You should use adb to create that directory and put a copy of arduplane from the build step in the directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:56
#: d1236c398e1f4b5dba262deef3be89c2
msgid "You will need some additional setup and configuration files as well. A copy of all of the required files is available here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:59
#: 51e3a75a84d74634a9b135bdf2283e37
msgid "https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/Tools/Frame_params/Parrot_Disco"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:61
#: 605bbee22bf74231abe11868e22e2599
msgid "You will need to modify the /etc/init.d/rcS_mode_default startup script to start ArduPilot. An example of a modified startup script to start ArduPilot if it is installed is available here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:65
#: 8c6f9afabe6a42df9c96d48c6aedfa09
msgid "https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/Frame_params/Parrot_Disco/rcS_mode_default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:67
#: a183f4a51ae740189f77595d18940384
msgid "you may find the 'Raw' button useful for downloading that file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:69
#: 31d98449e8cd4962af4619f01aa51340
msgid "That script will start ArduPilot is there is a start_ardupilot.sh script in the APM directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:72
#: ac616223b638446c8d7c254bb48a6896
msgid "You will also need to install the start_ardupilot.sh script. A copy of a suitable script is here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:75
#: 6d3d91d68efc45c2b272a08d955a4062
msgid "https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/Frame_params/Parrot_Disco/start_ardupilot.sh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:77
#: e1dda3ab2c7c465c859da4d0707cba27
msgid "that starts the Disco FAN and then loops running ArduPilot. The loop is so you can restart ArduPilot with a MAVLink preflight-reboot request from your GCS without rebooting the Disco."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:81
#: e90c84e3b5ff4c9a8675081abf131408
msgid "The startup script assumes that your Disco appears on the 192.168.42.0/24 network for WiFi and 192.168.43.0/24 network for USB networking. It tells ArduPilot to announce itself as a MAVLink device on those two networks. It will pick up the first MAVLink capable ground station that connects on UDP port 14550 on those networks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:88
#: 4d7ddd3170c047de9eed2d220a6b33a7
msgid "Ground Station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:90
#: 8aabb7948b12457cbb62d5f2372c66b1
msgid "For configuring your Disco you will need a ground station software package (GCS). There are several choices for use with Disco:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:93
#: f0405bab33344ab3a80a204138acbbd7
msgid "MissionPlanner (windows only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:94
#: 41140b264c174a8cbbb5e984d55d9b37
msgid "APM Planner (cross platform)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:95
#: bc2518db74cc4e92a7b242dc758c6ce5
msgid "QGroundControl (cross platform)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:96
#: 449308d8e2034bc79c7075e3dc96a284
msgid "MAVProxy (cross platform, experts only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:98
#: ac4c697f041747bf8431122cb13b31c7
msgid "They are all capable of controlling all aspects of the Disco setup and flight, including autonomous missions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:102
#: bf25ce3c9f304f62bb272ef26395683b
msgid "Transmitter Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:104
#: 589703bd292a493caba3cfb86c044401
msgid "The usual way to fly a Disco with ArduPilot is with a SBUS receiver and matching transmitter. You can also fly without a transmitter, but that is only recommended for advanced users who are very familiar with automated flight control with ArduPilot. We hope to support the Disco WiFi based transmitter in ArduPilot in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:112
#: af971e7db87f45c8b9dde9c3c0abb352
msgid "The telemetry output option of many R/C receivers can interfere badly with the Disco WiFi. Make sure you do a R/C range check before flying and also check that your WiFi telemetry has sufficient range for your needs. Many R/C receivers with a telemetry option can disable the telemetry when binding. Please refer to your receiver documentation for details. It is recommended that you disable receiver telemetry if you find your WiFi telemetry link from the Disco is affected by your receiver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:122
#: 653cde0483ca435ab385da9cf17c62b2
msgid "Loading Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:124
#: 489e411765c34b6eb4bdc62b5be5fa0f
msgid "You will need to load a set of parameters suitable for the Disco using your GCS. A recommended set of parameters to start with is here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:127
#: e4349f6e16e04065a95f650169082864
msgid "https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/Frame_params/Parrot_Disco/Parrot_Disco.param"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:129
#: cfdf0d7dbc4e4fea82e87318fd813c04
msgid "you can download that file directly for loading into a GCS with this link:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:132
#: 899b936c2446436bb5ca9b9a8f81a921
msgid "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/master/Tools/Frame_params/Parrot_Disco/Parrot_Disco.param"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:135
#: 463d0754dd5b4f8aa3605772daa86e47
msgid "Compass Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:137
#: 7111033ab73b4505bbc732a42d82a13b
msgid "You need to calibrate the compass in your Disco before you fly. This must be done with the hatch in place due to the magnetic catch on the hatch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:141
#: 32950829afd24282b74701b90edf7530
msgid "Each GCS choice has an option to start a compass calibration. Please choose on-board compass calibration for your GCS and follow the prompts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:145
#: d17343a49ebd4ab7a79130eea644ec6d
msgid "Note that you may find you need to raise COMPASS_CAL_FIT to allow successful calibration of the Disco, as the magnetic setup of the Disco hardware is not ideal and won't produce a perfect fit. We recommend setting COMPASS_CAL_FIT to 20."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:151
#: 3c6db99767104801b4bc7dbe6876013b
msgid "Accelerometer Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:153
#: d307b0272ae641cbb966d1d6a6fc8101
msgid "You also need to perform an accelerometer calibration. Please follow the prompts in your GCS for the accelerometer calibration procedure. This will only need to be performed once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:158
#: d6e1e6ee219343ef90405b7f1e6148a8
msgid "Airspeed Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:160
#: bfe01c9d2bd8477293671e5c8d8db71b
msgid "Before each flight you should perform an airspeed offset calibration as the airspeed sensor will vary in its zero value between power cycles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:164
#: 3686158e0ebe40ae8cf23706378c6eee
msgid "You should loosely cover the pitot tube that is built into the power switch and choose the pre-flight airspeed calibration option in your GCS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:169
#: 9c936f3ce89b476a946da475f48ebb82
msgid "Stabilisation Check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:171
#: 6156700f97744d559512bb0787056172
msgid "Before each flight you should check the stabilization of the Disco by changing to FBWA mode and checking the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:174
#: 0146bfe60a254495be14277656ca2343
msgid "roll the Disco to the right. The right elevon should go down, the left elevon should go up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:176
#: cbd59d0716df4ce79f133504cc825865
msgid "roll the Disco to the left. The left elevon should go down, the right elevon should go up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:178
#: 5fc4af7f00bf4db8a783645740740742
msgid "pitch the nose up. Both elevons should go down"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:179
#: 00f305d471094b2d94634d5c218334d6
msgid "pitch the nose down. Both elevons should go up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:181
#: be38df0dccc148959b01ad68557adc83
msgid "Next you should check for correct transmitter control with the Disco held level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:184
#: 42e3ca7b250e44468af7826994b2db90
msgid "input right roll on the transmitter. The left elevon should go down and the right elevon should go up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:186
#: fac4520e94714b1abc5be3b514e4c44d
msgid "input left roll on the transmitter. The right elevon should go down and the left elevon should go up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:188
#: a7290aca0e6343349cad26b38892c060
msgid "pull back on the pitch (elevator) stick on the transmitter. Both elevons should go up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:190
#: 86ff7d46424d419ca9004ab8749c7186
msgid "push forward on the pitch (elevator) stick on the transmitter. Both elevons should go down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:194
#: 160a8f909a68490992ef807fde05d770
msgid "Takeoff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:196
#: b0700bbeb492444ca8627f6fc5316bf8
msgid "The Disco has a very low stall speed which makes it easy to launch in a wide variety of ways. Some recommended ways are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:199
#: 89715dcb971b4ab08a50e3869711cb10
msgid "a side launch where you hold a wing close to the fuselage, and launch the aircraft forward. An example is shown here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:205
#: 0600b3c2c708457f967a38766182b793
msgid "a forward throw launch, as shown here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:210
#: 46ff70bcd01b40399161fc0f3c04152d
msgid "Always launch into the wind, and be careful to keep your hand clear of the propeller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:213
#: 484f46d1c30e4831b2ed6e0e28bfc34e
msgid "Also note that you can configure Disco for \"shake to start\", to start the motor when the airframe senses a shaking motion. That is set by the TKOFF_THR_MINACC=4 parameter in the parameter file linked above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:217
#: c3b49dd30ca54c0e8af39c1f302a3f22
msgid "You can see a \"shake to start\" example here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:224
#: 04655eb95b074f4a825a80ecb178aade
msgid "Flight Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:226
#: 8ddfff15cb414155bb0aab6c9bc7628a
msgid "For general stabilised flight FBWA mode is recommended. This is also good for takeoffs and landings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:229
#: 1d2e4515c48249cc89512db2a15b1a22
msgid "For longer distance FPV flying CRUISE mode is recommended as it will hold airspeed, height above ground and ground course."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:232
#: f56e50d4bf5247a7a17af44a5aa17363
msgid "You should also setup your transmitter for easy access to RTL mode to bring the plane home if you need to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:236
#: cfe4d40f43044ada84957f5a75bb5beb
msgid "Manual Landing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:238
#: b735c073d3f54625af70a1eb600dbbc5
msgid "To land manually FBWA mode is recommended. Just point the plane in the direction you want to land and drop the throttle. To come in more steeply push the pitch stick away. To perform a nice flare pull back a small amount on the pitch stick just before touchdown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:243
#: 3a48e2c10d424f3cbc69ee7a9765f3b4
msgid "APM:Plane will automatically put the nose down a couple of degrees when at zero throttle to keep the airspeed up. You can set how much nose down it uses at zero throttle with the STAB_PITCH_DOWN parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:248
#: 1d970b5ef4224d84ae4b3d4b47a0500d
msgid "Make sure you land with zero throttle or you risk breaking the propeller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:252
#: 6dd61648c6e740d190ca94332aa12f37
msgid "AUTO Landing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:254
#: 72ddfc05e8e242f08e7cd32eb78b2ed9
msgid "When using an AUTO mission you can place a NAV_LAND waypoint where you want to land, with a target altitude of zero meters. You also need to place an approach waypoint about 200 meters before the NAV_LAND point, about 30 meters above the ground. The Disco will automatically flare and cut the motor as it approaches the landing point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:260
#: a0f0bf3e17fa41b1a43e7ca23fef2a3c
msgid "Note that the Sonar used on the Disco for landing flare detection does have a tendency to sometimes produce false positives. That can cause the Disco to flare early in the landing as it thinks it is close to the ground. Because the Disco has such good glide characteristics this doesn't result in a crash, but it does cause it to land well short of the target position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:268
#: 1627978f4e1b4fbda2f7f9c3d0e1d866
msgid "Log Files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:270
#: d486035e2d244e128222b4ca459c5a7a
msgid "There are two types of log files for the Disco with ArduPilot. The first is a \"tlog\" which is stored by your GCS software on your ground station. The second is a \"DF\" log, which is stored on board the Disco."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:274
#: 22d10f6ee03a40b79f72c634d6163351
msgid "The log directory is /data/ftp/internal_000/APM/logs and can be accessed by ftp. Just enter a URL like ftp://192.168.42.1/ in Windows Explorer if using Windows to view the storage on the Disco and access log files. These files have a \".bin\" extension (for binary log file)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:280
#: 4bdf6acc30034d8bb18f6ea6d99ee34d
msgid "The C.H.U.C.K Autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:282
#: 0f3d75b417e840db95c049eb2b1b4cc2
msgid "The heart of the Disco is the C.H.U.C.K autopilot, an orange box which is a general purpose autopilot. It is perfectly possible to use the C.H.U.C.K in a different airframe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airframe-disco.rst:286
#: 2eb723092c0d44a88158dd77e83679e5
msgid "For more information on using C.H.U.C.K with ArduPilot please see the :ref:`C.H.U.C.K AutoPilot <common-CHUCK-overview>`"
msgstr ""
